Counties ending with “County”
SELECT
    MEMBER_COUNTY,
    COUNT(*) AS RECORD_COUNT
FROM [dbo].[SourceTable]
WHERE LOWER(LTRIM(RTRIM(MEMBER_COUNTY))) LIKE '% county'
GROUP BY MEMBER_COUNTY
ORDER BY MEMBER_COUNTY;
This finds values such as:
Dallas County
Orange County
Verify the two exceptions
SELECT
    MEMBER_COUNTY,
    COUNT(*) AS RECORD_COUNT
FROM [dbo].[SourceTable]
WHERE MEMBER_COUNTY IN (
    'City And County Of Honolulu',
    'Town And County Of Nantucket'
)
GROUP BY MEMBER_COUNTY;
These should remain unchanged because “County” is part of the official name, not simply a suffix to remove.
Review the country transformation
SELECT
    MEMBER_COUNTRY,
    COUNT(*) AS RECORD_COUNT
FROM [dbo].[SourceTable]
GROUP BY MEMBER_COUNTRY
ORDER BY MEMBER_COUNTRY;
This should show the original values, including USA, blanks, Mexico, and any other countries.
